# rclone filter rules for the two-way KB sync (rclone/ntu_kb_sync.sh).
#
# Copy this to `rclone/ntu-kb.filter` and edit it for your own tree. That file
# is git-ignored, because an exclude list is a map of your folder structure and
# of what you deliberately keep off the cloud -- not something to publish.
#
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom and the FIRST match wins, so every exclude
# has to precede the catch-all `+ /**` at the bottom. A leading `/` anchors the
# pattern to the sync root; without one it matches at any depth.
#
# IMPORTANT: rclone bisync hashes this file. Editing it puts the next run into a
# "filters changed" abort that can only be cleared with:
#     rclone/ntu_kb_sync.sh --resync
# That is expected, not a bug.

# --- Bulk: not worth pushing to the cloud, and not wanted on a tablet --------
# Old material you never open on the go. Often already gitignored.
- /archive/**
# Scratch space.
- /99-dump/**
# Large regenerable corpora (test data, datasets, build inputs).
# - /path/to/large-test-data/**

# --- Data that must not leave the machine ------------------------------------
# Anything containing third-party personal data: raw chat exports, class
# rosters, contact dumps. Exclude these deliberately and keep them excluded.
# - /path/to/sources/raw/**

# --- Deliberately out of scope ----------------------------------------------
# Machine-generated state that is rewritten often and never annotated by hand.
# Syncing it only manufactures conflicts.
# - /path/to/state/**

# --- Repo and tooling internals ---------------------------------------------
# If the synced tree is a git repo, never sync .git: bisync writing a
# conflict-renamed file inside it would corrupt the repo.
- .git/**
- .gitignore
- .gitattributes
- .claude/**
- AGENTS.md

# --- Derived files and caches ------------------------------------------------
- __pycache__/**
- *.pyc
- .venv/**
- node_modules/**
- .pytest_cache/**
- .mypy_cache/**
- *.egg-info/**
- .DS_Store
# C compile artifacts.
- a.out
- *.o
- *.dSYM/**
# Affinity source files: tens of MB each, only the exported PDF matters.
- *.af
- *.af~lock~

# --- Everything else syncs both ways ----------------------------------------
# Consider deliberately INCLUDING large PDFs you want to annotate, even ones
# your .gitignore excludes for size reasons -- they are the whole point.
+ /**
